cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  openplan-bench: a reproducible benchmarking harness and leaderboard for the
  OpenPlan Labs planners
message: >-
  If you use these benchmarks or this harness in academic work, please cite it,
  and please state the suite, the results file date and the machine — a number
  without those is not a result.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Erwin
    family-names: Lejeune
    email: erwin.lejeune15@gmail.com
repository-code: https://github.com/openplan-labs/openplan-bench
url: https://openplan-labs.github.io/openplan-bench/
abstract: >-
  openplan-bench runs the OpenPlan Labs planners over shared problem sets and
  publishes the results as a leaderboard. It covers classical PDDL planning via
  jupyddl and multi-agent path finding via pymapf and cuda-planning, behind a
  uniform adapter interface. Every requested run produces exactly one record,
  including runs that time out, error, or could not be attempted, so coverage
  figures are not inflated by omission. Each record carries the machine, the
  package versions, the seed and the harness commit that produced it. Solutions
  are accepted only after validation, and an instance counts as
  solved only when every seed solved it.
keywords:
  - benchmarking
  - reproducibility
  - automated planning
  - PDDL
  - multi-agent path finding
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-08-21'
